Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/apiplant/idol-rs
Description: one image to a 3D Gaussian splat on NVIDIA GPUs (Rust, CUDA)
 idol turns one picture of an object into a 3D Gaussian splat (a
 standard 3DGS .ply): it removes the background, frames the object and
 generates up to a million Gaussians, including the sides the picture
 never showed. `idol serve` adds an HTTP API and a built-in web UI with
 a 3D viewer. Needs an NVIDIA GPU (Ampere or newer); the model files are
 downloaded on first use. It links the CUDA 13 runtime (libcudart,
 libcublas, libnvrtc), which is not packaged by Debian or Ubuntu: install
 it from NVIDIA's CUDA repository. libcuda1 (installed by the NVIDIA
 driver package) satisfies the driver link only.
